WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.532
A six-line poem uses a connected idea, vivid words, fitting rhythm and purposeful

00:00:05.532 --> 00:00:09.224
sound patterns. A thoughtful response explains its central theme.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:14.758
Why does a poet choose an image such as “silver moon”? Answer: It helps a reader

00:00:14.758 --> 00:00:15.644
picture the scene.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:21.415
Compose six original lines about a Ghanaian place and explain the value expressed by

00:00:21.415 --> 00:00:22.125
your poem.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.681
Why it works: An image makes an idea vivid.
